# Review: CodeIndex

code-index meets its spec closely, and its test suite tracks the spec's own case lists almost line for line.
`Store.test.ts`, `Indexer.test.ts`, `typescript.test.ts`, `package.test.ts`, `Mdl.test.ts`, `Reasoner.test.ts`,
`agreement.test.ts`, the MCP tests and `Watch.test.ts` cover the commit protocol, version and backend resets,
incremental passes, import edges, call sites, spec facts, ordered reasoning and the MCP tools. The gaps are small:
`stats` counts derived graphs from a recorded summary and per-graph native counts rather than a grouped SPARQL count
(F-11.5); `workspace/Log.ts` opens a SQLite database of its own outside `Store` (F-1.3); `Indexer.Options` takes
`reasoners` and has no `DEFAULT_REASONER`. A few behaviours have no test: unreadable files reported as skipped, a
`Package` node surviving a lone reindex, the sub-millisecond type step and a failed watch pass.

The review parser lists only modules whose ids have no `/`, so `worker/*` and `mcp/*` are not judged as modules;
their behaviour is judged through F-4, F-8, F-10 and F-11. The `F-11` fence is not closed before `F-12`, but F-12's
requirements still parse.

Of 65 items: 56 done, 6 untested, 2 partial, 1 diverged, 0 missing. (Counts include the 7 `T-*` tests.)

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

